WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
You stop at a market stall
and ask: how much is this?

2
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.230
You never meant to buy it.

3
00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.820
You were only curious.

4
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:12.020
The Mishnah, a key text of Jewish law,
has something to say about that question.

5
00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:16.790
So can asking for a price you
never mean to pay really be a sin?

6
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:19.920
In this mission, you'll read
the Torah's laws on lending,

7
00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:22.680
and trace how they
developed over centuries.

8
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.380
Then you'll test ancient laws on
just weights against modern shopping.

9
00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.040
Your mission: find out what
Jewish law asks of buyers,

10
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:34.850
sellers and lenders, right
down to a single question.
